 	  If unsure, say "n".
 
+config ZONE_MOVABLE_CMA
+	bool "Contiguous Memory Allocator by ZONE_MOVABLE"
+	select CMA
+	depends on MMU && MEDIATEK_SOLUTION
+	default y
+	help
+	  This enable the support of ZONE MOVALBE Contiguous Memory Allocator.
+	  Traditional CMA is based on a "fallback logic". The system takes
+	  CMA memory only when it runs out of normal memory and makes the
+	  utilization of CMA low. With ZONE_MOVABLE_CMA, we use a movable zone
+	  to manage CMA memory, all movable pages will be allocated from this
+	  zone first and make utilization of CMA memory high.
+
